--- Overview
ghpr and pconn no longer search the current directory for config files by default. They now look only in their own user configuration directory, and they read a file from the current directory only when it's named with --config.

--- Key Changes
  * ghpr
    * Added searchPath(explicit). It returns cmdconfig.SearchPathUserDirs("ghpr") by default and cmdconfig.SearchPath("ghpr"), which includes ., when --config is set.
    * configSpec now uses searchPath, and --config help text, README.md and cmdusage.go are updated to match.
    * Tests cover the search path contents, ignoring a cwd config.yaml/ghpr.yaml by default, reading a named cwd file, and falling back to ~/.config/ghpr.
  * pconn
    * Added configSpecFor(*cmdconfig.FilesFlag) and searchPath(explicit). configSpec now uses the global flag.
    * connect now builds its spec from its own --config flag, so a relative name given to that flag is still found in the current directory.
    * --config help, README.md, config.md and cmdusage.go now give the per-OS default location (~/Library/Application Support/pconn on macOS, otherwise $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pconn or ~/.config/pconn). They also fix the stale pconn.yaml default.
    * Tests cover the search path, the "no configuration file found" error when only a cwd file exists, reading a named cwd file, the user directory lookup, and configSpecFor.
  * Dependencies: bumped cloudeng.io/cmdutil to v0.0.0-20261027172419-c2cb239e8127 in both modules, which provides SearchPathUserDirs.

--- Breaking Changes
  * A config.yaml (or ghpr.yaml) in the current directory is no longer picked up automatically. Users who rely on one must pass --config config.yaml or move it to the tool's user configuration directory.
  * pconn now fails with "no configuration file found" if the only config file is in the current directory.

